  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1054 PM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nThe upper ridge will not move much during the day Thursday. Light \nESE winds will continue behind a \"cold\" front which will bring some \nwelcome relief to our recent stretch of triple-digit temperatures. \nHigh will top out in the low-to-mid 90s across the area. Another \nslightly weaker shortwave will move through during the evening hours \nyielding generally the same setup as the previous evening. Forcing \nwill not be as strong and 500 mb winds will be slightly more due \nnortherly than northwesterly, however once again DCAPE between 1000-\n1500 J/kg and PWATs approaching 1.5 inches in spots will bring about \nthe same strong wind and heavy downpour threats throughout much of \nthe forecast area. These should again taper off around midnight. The \nridge will slightly weaken, but move back eastward Friday into \nthe weekend, thereby inhibiting any additional monsoonal moisture \nover our area. PoPs look be limited to none from then on into next\nweek and temperatures will gradually increase again to at or near\ntriple-digits.",
